# CVE-2026-67422 (pymdown-extensions, HIGH, ReDoS)
#
# Only findable inside a vendored dependency's own docs-build tooling:
# go/vendor/github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-go/Pipfile.lock.
# testcontainers-go is a test-only Go dependency (its own package files are
# never imported outside internal/store's *_test.go); its Pipfile.lock is a
# Python mkdocs/pymdown-extensions pin used to build ITS OWN documentation
# site upstream, checked in only because `go mod vendor` mirrors the whole
# module source tree, not just the .go files sudo-logger actually compiles.
# There is no code path in this repo that installs or runs this Python
# tooling. testcontainers-go v0.44.0 (latest available at the time this was
# added) still pins pymdown-extensions 10.21.3; the fix (11.0.1) has not
# been adopted upstream yet. Re-check this line when bumping
# testcontainers-go again — remove it once upstream picks up the fix.
CVE-2026-67422
